<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NB - no buyer T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH		PREV</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	     12/9 D	 April		10/8 D</p>
<p> May		 12/9 D	 May		  10/8 D</p>
<p> July	    2 D/even	 July		  4/7 P</p>
<p> August	   10/15 P	 August	    10/13 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	    1.5/1 D	 March		 4/2 D</p>
<p> May		 11/8 D	 May		 16/15 D</p>
<p> July	     16/10 D	 July		18/17 D</p>
<p> August	     7/3 D	 August	     10/6 D</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	  130/115 D	 April	   170/150 D</p>
<p> May	    160/130 D	 May	     200/150 D</p>
<p> July	   175/130 D	 July	    215/185 D</p>
<p> August	 170/120 D	 August	  200/180 D</p>
